userStories.description:
**Goal** — Provide the repo identity, bounded flow job rows and pure cost calculations needed by the overview route.

**Motivation** — F1-F5 built and verified the engine; live flows 13 and 14 were followed with SQL, `gh` and a polling script, because nothing in the web app shows a flow.

**Approach** — Cross-module reads go through services (`.nax/rules/api-data.md`): the repo identity through a new `FleetReposService.findIdentity(id)`, the ticket ref through the existing `TicketsService.findRefsByIds` (`TicketsModule` is already imported by the flows module). The flow's jobs are read by the flow step repository, which already reads the flow's `FleetJob` rows (`latestJob`, `latestJobForStep`); the new `listFlowJobs(flowId, limit)` follows that precedent. `FleetJob.flowFeatureId` has no Prisma relation, so the feature name comes from the flow's own features (id to name map), not from a join. Ticket resolution and the feature name map themselves are composed in US-003.

Unknown cost follows the design ("`AGENT`, `PLAN`, `REVIEW` and `FIX` jobs may report no cost"): a job whose `command` is `AGENT`, `PLAN`, `REVIEW` or `FIX`, whose state is in `TERMINAL_STATES`, and whose `costSpentUsd + costCarriedUsd` is zero. The page text is `cap excludes N jobs with unknown cost`. Use the existing TERMINAL_STATES from jobs/job-state.ts, not a divergent state list. Use Prisma.Decimal from the generated client for exact addition and zero comparison; never floating-point money.

Jobs are capped at the newest 500 (by `queuedAt` then `id`), returned oldest first, with `truncated: true` when the flow has more. The live flows have 12 jobs. The unknown-cost count covers the returned jobs. The reusable repository method takes a caller-supplied limit; US-003 passes 500. Select newest rows by queuedAt desc/id desc, detect overflow with a bounded extra row or equivalent bounded/count read, retain only limit rows, then return oldest-first including ascending id ties. Return only rows of the requested flow and both costs as 4-place strings. `findIdentity` is a narrow repo service projection returning null if absent, following `findReviewRepo`; do not alter existing methods or expose credentials.

Add listFlowJobs cases to `test/integration/fleet/fleet-flow-step.repository.integration.spec.ts`, findIdentity cases to `src/fleet/repos/fleet-repos.service.spec.ts`, and pure helper cases beside flow-overview.ts. Keep existing interface methods and tests unchanged.

**Scope** — In: repo identity service method, step repository type/interface/read, pure decimal total and unknown-cost count. Out: overview DTO/controller/service composition and ticket lookups (US-003), web formatting/grouping (US-004/007), Paging the overview's jobs beyond the newest 500; the overview reports `truncated` instead. Changing any flow step, state transition or stop rule in the API.

**Interface**
```ts
// apps/api/src/fleet/repos/fleet-repos.service.ts
findIdentity(id: string): Promise<{ provider: string; owner: string; name: string } | null>

// apps/api/src/fleet/flows/domain/fleet-flow-step.domain.ts (IFleetFlowStepRepository) + Prisma implementation
listFlowJobs(flowId: string, limit: number): Promise<{ jobs: FlowJobRow[]; truncated: boolean }>
interface FlowJobRow {
  id: string; flowFeatureId: string | null; flowStep: string | null; command: string; state: string;
  costSpentUsd: string; costCarriedUsd: string; queuedAt: Date; finishedAt: Date | null;
}

// apps/api/src/fleet/flows/flow-overview.ts (pure)
export const UNKNOWN_COST_COMMANDS: readonly string[]   // AGENT PLAN REVIEW FIX
export function totalCostUsd(row: FlowJobRow): string    // costSpentUsd + costCarriedUsd, 4 decimals
export function countUnknownCost(rows: FlowJobRow[]): number
```

**Goal** — Add the project-scoped overview read route that composes repo identity, ticket ref, jobs and unknown-cost count.

**Motivation** — The design (`docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-04-fleet-flow-design.md`, G8 and "Status page") calls for a page that shows each feature's current step, its jobs, its PR and the cost against the cap.

**Approach** — One new read route, `GET /api/projects/:slug/flows/:flowId/overview` (`fleet.flow.read`), answers what the record does not hold: the repo identity, the flow ticket's ref, the flow's jobs, and the unknown-cost count. It lives in a new `ProjectFlowOverviewController` (`@Controller('projects/:slug/flows')`) and a new `FleetFlowOverviewService`, so the constructors of `ProjectFlowsController` and `FleetFlowsService` do not change. Both are registered in `flows.module.ts`.

Cross-module reads go through services (`.nax/rules/api-data.md`): the repo identity through a new `FleetReposService.findIdentity(id)`, the ticket ref through the existing `TicketsService.findRefsByIds` (`TicketsModule` is already imported by the flows module). The flow's jobs are read by the flow step repository, which already reads the flow's `FleetJob` rows (`latestJob`, `latestJobForStep`); the new `listFlowJobs(flowId, limit)` follows that precedent. `FleetJob.flowFeatureId` has no Prisma relation, so the feature name comes from the flow's own features (id to name map), not from a join.

`FleetFlowOverviewService.overview(projectId, flowId)` fences the flow with `FleetFlowsService.get`, then builds `FleetFlowOverviewDto` from `findIdentity`, `findRefsByIds` and `listFlowJobs(flowId, 500)`, naming each job's feature from the flow's features. Missing/cross-project flows throw 404 `fleet.flows.notFound` before downstream reads. Null ticketId skips findRefsByIds; absent ticket-map entries and missing repos become null. Convert dates to ISO, preserve null finishedAt, use totalCostUsd and countUnknownCost only over returned rows, and propagate truncated.

`ProjectFlowOverviewController` carries the same class decorators as `ProjectFlowsController`: `@ApiTags('fleet')`, `@ApiBearerAuth()`, `@ApiParam({ name: 'slug' })`, `@UseGuards(ProjectMembershipGuard, RequiresGuard)`; the route has `@ApiOperation` and `@ApiResponse` for 200 (`FleetFlowOverviewDto`), 403 and 404. Every DTO field has `@ApiProperty`. Return `JsonResponse.Ok` of the service result.

Register the two new classes without replacing existing providers/controllers. Add no-DB service/controller tests in fleet-flow-overview.spec.ts; any module-compilation checks remain co-located unit tests. The endpoint e2e file gains the route's 200 and 404 paths, leaving existing cases as they are. Regenerate root `openapi.json` with `bun run api:export-spec`.

**Scope** — In: overview DTOs, service orchestration, guarded controller, DI registration and generated API contract. Out: repository reads/cost helper implementation (US-002), web contracts and callers (US-004/005), modifications to existing controller/service constructors, Paging the overview's jobs beyond the newest 500; the overview reports `truncated` instead. Changing any flow step, state transition or stop rule in the API.

**Interface**
```ts
// apps/api/src/fleet/flows/fleet-flow-overview.service.ts
class FleetFlowOverviewService {
  overview(projectId: string, flowId: string): Promise<FleetFlowOverviewDto>
}

// apps/api/src/fleet/flows/project-flow-overview.controller.ts
@Controller('projects/:slug/flows') class ProjectFlowOverviewController {
  @Get(':flowId/overview') @Requires('fleet.flow.read') overview(flowId, ctx)
}

// apps/api/src/fleet/flows/dto/fleet-flow-overview.dto.ts
class FleetFlowOverviewDto {
  repo: { provider: string; owner: string; name: string } | null;  // null when the repo row is gone
  ticketRef: string | null;        // from TicketsService.findRefsByIds, null when the flow has no ticket
  jobs: FleetFlowJobDto[];         // newest 500 by queuedAt then id, returned oldest first
  truncated: boolean;
  unknownCostCount: number;
}
class FleetFlowJobDto {
  id: string;
  feature: string | null;          // the flow feature's name for flowFeatureId, null when flowFeatureId is null
  step: string | null;             // flowStep
  command: string;
  state: string;
  costUsd: string;                 // totalCostUsd
  queuedAt: string;                // ISO
  finishedAt: string | null;       // ISO
}
```
